A||||5||kempo||New GrandAm Motor 3.4Supercharged||||1||
Z||000000||kempo||10-03-2001||01:33 PM||||I am looking for information on this new engine.  I was going to swap out the 2.8 with a '95 Camaro 3.4, but then searched around and saw that the new Grand Am's will have a 3.4L Supercharged v6 stock, which got me thinking...  Would the swap work?  Or should I stick with the Camaro 3.4 and see what I can do with it?  Any info helps!  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/kempsig.jpg"> <BR>87 Fiero GT / 5 Speed<BR>86 Fiero 2m4 - FOR SALE||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||10-03-2001||02:02 PM||||Check out <A HREF="http://www.grandamgt.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.grandamgt.com</A>  for more info.  Right now there is a supercharger kit available for the 3400SFI in 99+ Grand Ams.  It's supposed to put it up to about 260HP.  It just did hit the market and runs about $3500.  Rumour has it this engine will be available from the factory in 2002 or 2003, but nothing definate, yet (that I've heard).<P>The 3400SFI is a good engine (that's what's in my '99 Grand Am), but it's mounts are different thatn the earlier 3.4 and 2.8.  A few people on here have done 3400SFI swaps, so you might try doing a search.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jaei Sun||10-03-2001||03:55 PM||||Here's my problem with GM.  Now why the hell is it going to take over a year to impliment this supercharger/engine into this car?  If this was a foreign company it would be out in a matter of months!  RSX for example... that thing was out pretty fast.  I have the same problem with Chrysler and their PT cruiser.  It has been for sale for how many years now and they still haven't "corrected" the underpowered issue that 95% of the buyers (and magizines)  say they have with it.  Again if this was foreign company that would have been corrected in a few months time.<P><BR>And why the hell was ~93 the last year you could get a MANUAL with a v6 engine in ANY FWD GM CAR????  Don't these asses think that people want a 5-speed Grand AM?  <p>[This message has been edited by Jaei Sun (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||10-03-2001||05:18 PM||||I'll be strapping one of them on my 3400 soon enough!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||10-03-2001||06:29 PM||||OK here's a silly question, If they are making a kit that bolts on to a 3.4 will it bolt up to a 2.8? Or a 3.1?||||reg||5
Z||000005||Formula88||10-03-2001||07:51 PM||||I'm wondering that myself, Orief.  It's designed for the 3400SFI, but is a straight bolt on to the stock engine, so you'd have to fabricate mounts, and interface between the blower and the plenum, not to mention the belt drive, since our 2.8 isn't serpentine.  But really, it shouldn't be too much harder than any of the other swaps done out there.  <P>Also, rumour has it a 6-speed manual will be out in a year or two.  If that sucker will bolt to the 3400SFI SC, then I think we have found a new hi-perf manual tranny for our Fieros!  <P>Again, <A HREF="http://www.grandamgt.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.grandamgt.com</A>  is the best source for info on the 99+ Grand Ams and the 3400SFI info.  They even have a board devoted just to the supercharger.  A few members on there were involved with the development of it.  They have a great search function (just like here) and most of the questions you might have (unless they're Fiero specific) have already been answered (just like here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  There's even a few Fiero enthusiasts on there!  (including me).  I post under Formula88 there as well.<P>Pontiac has even recognized their site and sponsored some of their shows.  A great source of info.<P>I've also heard that the next generation of Grand Prix GTP won't be supercharged, but that's because it'll have more horsepower normally aspirated than the current SC engine!  I'm thinking that might be a great engine for us, too.  Just a matter of time...||||reg||1
